# Generated by render.sh — regenerate with `bash render.sh <file.html>`, don't commit.
# The PNGs are ~200dpi on-screen review crops, not print deliverables.
*.png
_*.html

# ...except the brand marks the posters actually link to.
!_assets/logo-full-white.png

# Dish photography is DATA, not code (CLAUDE.md: "Dish price, photo, composition
# -> neither repo"). The heroes are 5 MB each and live in the master photo library:
#   Google Drive shared folder (new shots) + ~/Desktop/Shishka rest/Menu/Links/ (archive)
# Drop the file into _assets/ under the name the poster's <img src> expects.
_assets/hero-*.png

# PDFs are already ignored repo-wide by the root .gitignore, so nothing rendered
# here is tracked at all. The HTML is the source of truth; `bash render.sh x.html`
# rebuilds the print-ready PDF in one command. Send the PDF to the print shop from
# your own machine — A3 297x420 mm, print at 100% / "actual size", no scaling.
